INSERT INTO public.segments (id, lecture_id, start_s, end_s, transcript, slide_text, embedding) VALUES ('9a8db860-64b4-4235-a1d8-b5ae95ee7768', '9736166c-3585-4b19-ac9b-48b30e3242ac', 2080, 2142, 'So now we have to justify runtime for this algorithm. And that''s like actually not 100% obvious from the way I''ve written it here. There''s no for loop. But what do I do? Well, in some sense, if my runtime is a function s, well, for one thing, if my array has one element Well, my runtime, you know, it might be 7, it might be 23, but at the end of the day, it only does one thing. It just returns i. Right? So in other words, it''s theta of 1. This isn''t terribly insightful, but what else do we know? Well, when I call my function, I call it recursively on one smaller index, and then I do a constant amount of work. So I know that s of n is equal to s of n minus 1 plus theta of 1. Right? I do a little bit of extra computation on top of that. Anybody guess what this total runtime is going to be? Yes? Yeah, order n. Right? So let''s say that we hypothesize that this takes n time.', 'in key order
