INSERT INTO public.segments (id, lecture_id, start_s, end_s, transcript, slide_text, embedding) VALUES ('01332400-508c-42bc-a6a2-a030e959c0ff', '9736166c-3585-4b19-ac9b-48b30e3242ac', 2636, 2698, 'OK. So I''m going to show that my merged array, 5, 6, 7, has 8 elements. And now I''m going to have two fingers at the end of my array. Which one should I put at the end of the merged guy? The 7 or the 9? The 9. The 9. Right. Thank you. Right? So now I can move my lower finger to the left. Right? Because I''ve already added that. Notice that I never need to look to the left of where my finger is because they''re already in sorted order. Right? Now what should I add? The 4 or the 7? The 7. The 7. The 8. And so on. Dot, dot, dot. Yeah? So that''s going to be the basic idea of the merged sort. I''m going to take two sorted lists. And I''m going to make a new sorted list, which is twice as long, by using two fingers. Moving from the end backward. OK. So that''s the basic intuition here. Indeed, there''s our sorted list. It''s stressing me out that there''s no 8, but I needed a power of 2.', 'in key order
